## Test 2 (zone-2 -> zone-3 in-session switch, reverse of §5.7's last step): PARTIALLY per literal instruction,
## core concern fully confirmed via an equivalent path

Attempted the LITERAL zone2->zone3 switch while module 4 (zone 3's single module) was the currently active
module (reached via the store's own "Change Location" -> Set From Map -> search "Sheikh Zayed Grand Mosque"
-> map-nudge -> Pick Location technique that reliably reaches zone 2). Result BOTH times attempted:

  [WARN] location: module not available for this location
  -> ZoneWarningDialog ("Sorry, this service is not available in your location" / "Please select another
     delivery location...") -> switch ABORTED, address unchanged (confirmed: a subsequent relaunch still
     fired store_direct_opened for zone 3, proving the address never actually moved).

Traced to `location_controller.dart`'s pre-existing (NEARS-1022, NOT part of this ticket's diff)
`_saveDataAndFirebaseConfig` availability guard: `zoneModules.any((m) => m.id == current.id &&
isModuleServiceable(m))` -- requires the EXACT same module id to be servable in the target zone. Module 4
(zone 3 only) is never present in zone 2's module list (confirmed via direct backend curl: zone 2's modules
are ids 1/2/3/5), so ANY switch carrying an active module 4 into zone 2 is symmetrically blocked by this
guard -- and by the same logic, carrying an active module 1/2/3/5 INTO zone 3 would be blocked identically.
This is a working-as-designed guard from a PRIOR ticket, confirmed via code and live reproduction, not a
regression from NEARS-3584's diff (module_controller.dart's `_autoSelectArmed` refactor doesn't touch this
guard's call site or predicate at all).

Attempting to reach a genuine "no module active" starting point specifically FROM the trimmed-hero screen (to
then attempt a clean zone2->zone3 switch through the same shared gate mechanism, matching Test 1's own
precondition) hit a session-specific dead end: the trimmed-hero's own back-stack treats a second back-press as
app-exit rather than the PopScope module-clear behavior observed elsewhere on the normal (multi-store) Home
-- exited the app outright once, requiring a relaunch. This is a back-stack observation on the trimmed-hero
screen specifically, not confirmed to be new (module_view.dart's PopScope logic is unchanged by this diff per
git diff) and out of THIS narrow scope to chase further.

CONCLUSION: the specific concern behind Test 2 -- "does the shared `_autoSelectArmed` gate, after this
ticket's if/else-if refactor, still correctly reach `consumeAutoSelectSingleModule()` (not just
`consumeAutoSelectDefaultModule()`)?" -- is fully and directly answered YES by Test 1 itself: the zone
454(no module)->zone 3(module 4) switch is the SAME gate, same code path (`_prepareModuleList`'s arm/consume
cycle), just entered via an address-change with a null starting module rather than a cold boot. It reached
the single-module arm correctly (hero rendered, store_auto_opened fired once, module_restored/
sector_auto_selected dual-fire semantics intact per fix-cycle-1/2's already-PASSed AC1). The LITERAL
zone2(module-active)->zone3 direction is blocked by an unrelated, pre-existing, symmetric guard before the
gate is ever reached -- this is expected product behavior, not a gap in this ticket's fix.

No seeded-fixture gap exists for either the doc's recipe (confirmed working end-to-end, just via the
